## Changed

- Decoupled provider-event consumption from sampling: invalidations now fork into the coordinator scope, so a blocked sample cannot prevent later invalidations from marking the lane stale/coalesced.
- Retained separate poll-deadline ownership; replacing a deadline cannot interrupt the sample it triggers.
- Expanded the fake provider with deterministic sample/transport gates and one-shot failures.
- Added deterministic coordinator coverage for snapshot authority, stale/coalesced samples, navigation authority, 3/5/8 polling, deadline reset, reconciliation delay, queue saturation, and failure continuation.
- Added one-attempt media-control coverage proving no retry timer is created and terminal disposal is exact-once. Server close is also asserted idempotent.

Files touched: `packages/music-core/session/coordinator.ts`, `packages/music-core/session/provider.ts`, `packages/music-core/tests/session-coordinator.test.ts`, `packages/music-core/tests/session-server.test.ts`, and `packages/music-core/tests/system-media.test.ts`.

